  "id": "ua-pulaski-technical-college-aas-emergency-medical-sciences",
  "major": "Emergency Medical Sciences",
  "notes": "Designed for students who wish to obtain a two-year degree while pursuing or after completing the Technical Certificate in EMS - Paramedic. Students are accepted into the paramedic program for fall entry. Approximately 40% of paramedic program coursework is delivered online. Paramedic classes are held on Mondays or Wednesdays with an occasional Friday (generally two Mondays each month); clinical time may be scheduled within program guidelines including weekdays, weekends, and nights. Current Arkansas licensure as an EMT is a prerequisite to enter this program. Minimum 2.00 cumulative GPA required for graduation. Additional prerequisite courses may be required if minimum placement test scores are not met. CATALOG PRESENTATION NOTE: General Education Semester Two lists 'Select three (3) of the following' with the nine listed courses and a 3-credit row value; the three selections are modeled as three 3-credit slots (9 credits), which reconciles with the semester header 'Complete all 12 Hours' (ENGL 10203 = 3 + three selections = 9).",
